
===== EpiLPS-MALA under SI misspecification (NegBin data) =====
Sampler: LPSMALA, 5000 iterations, 2000 burn-in, 3000 retained draws per fit
True SI: realised mean/sd 7.4992 / 3.4215 (requested 7.5 / 3.4), lags 0-30
Reporting hole(s) removed: 2020-07-08
Truth: true_R_epilps, 253 days, Rt 0.619 to 7.802
Seeding: I0 = 2000 on day 1 (NegBin draws from day 2)
Scoring days 2-253 (252 days), 100 replicates, shared across all SI settings

calibrating on the observed series (one MALA fit, also times the grid) ...

NegBin overdispersion on the observed series:
  rho = 17.36  (LPSMAP mode)  <- used to generate the data
  rho = 17.17  (LPSMALA posterior mean, diagnostic only)
  at mu = 1000: SD 242 (NegBin) vs 32 (Poisson), 7.7x the noise

simulated 100 / 100 replicates (0 diverged, 0 went extinct)
median final-day incidence 314

13 unique SI settings to fit (1 families x 13 moment settings;
  14 rows reported, the point the two sweeps share is fitted once per family)
100 replicates x 13 settings = 1300 LPSMALA fits

1 setting(s) miss the requested moments by more than 0.25. They are
fitted and reported, but grid_value overstates how wrong the SI really is,
so read them off realised_mean / realised_sd:
